305 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Widget/V<>/F 4/C[1 0 0]/FT/Tx/T(COMMENTS)/DV()/MK<</IF<</A[0 0]>>>>/DA(0 0 0 rg /Calibri 9 Tf)/AP<</N 304 0 R>>/Rect[64.60429 70.6084 561.2596 400.6237]/M(D:20260615102428-04'00')/BS 264 0 R/Ff 33558528/RV(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" style="font:9pt Calibri; text-align:left; text-valign:top; line-height:10.35pt; color:#000000" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="font-family:Calibri; line-height:10.35pt; font-size:9pt">CMTA Comments:</p><p style="font-family:Calibri; font-size:9pt" /><p style="font-family:Calibri; font-size:9pt">1. Provide vibration isolation for pumps and piping within 50 feet or 50 pipe diameters, whichever is greater.  See specifications for details.</p><p style="font-size:9pt; font-family:Calibri" /><p style="font-family:Calibri; font-size:9pt">2. Provide valve and trim as per the details on the design documents.</p><p style="font-size:9pt; font-family:Calibri" /><p style="font-family:Calibri; font-size:9pt">3. Pumps shall meet all pressure and flow characteristics as per the design documents.</p><p style="font-size:9pt; font-family:Calibri" /><p style="font-family:Calibri; font-size:9pt">4. Contractor to provide the differential pressure at the tie in to the risers in full flow condition, as per the design documents, and provide to the manufacturer to ensure the proper head is obtained to ensure full flow throughout the system. </p><p style="font-family:Calibri; font-size:9pt" /></body>)/DS(font: Calibri 9pt; text-align:left; line-height:10.35pt; color:#000000)>>
endobj

